# The fleet flatpak set — baked into the installer ISO by Titanoboa (system scope,
# /var/lib/flatpak) so first boot is fully offline and an opilas home reset never
# loses an app. One list for one image: flatpaks/{student,staff}.list are gone.
#
# Rationale, checked against workstation-ostree-config packages/silverblue.yaml on
# the f44 branch (the config quay.io/fedora-ostree-desktops/silverblue:44 is built
# from). Silverblue ships gnome-disk-utility, gnome-software, nautilus, ptyxis,
# gnome-system-monitor and gnome-control-center, and from common.yaml only unzip.
# It ships NO PDF viewer, image viewer, archive manager, calculator or text editor —
# so TextEditor is not a duplicate, it is the only text editor, and without
# Papers/Loupe/FileRoller/Calculator a student cannot open a PDF, view an image or
# extract an archive outside the CLI.
#
# No terminal flatpak: ptyxis is already in the image as an RPM (Fedora's default
# terminal since F41 — GTK4 and container-aware for toolbx/distrobox, which is the
# point on an atomic desktop). It is restricted to wheel, not added here.
#
# adw-gtk3 + adw-gtk3-dark are runtimes, not apps: GIMP, Inkscape and Audacity are
# GTK3 flatpaks and don't pick up the host theme without them. Bluefin ships both
# for the same reason.
#
# NEVER ADD — deliberately blocked, don't "helpfully" put them back:
#   com.github.tchx84.Flatseal        (sandbox permission editor)
#   com.mattjakeman.ExtensionManager  (GNOME extension installer)
#   io.github.flattool.Warehouse      (flatpak manager / mass uninstall)
#   io.github.kolunmi.Bazaar          (alternative app store)
#   io.gitlab.adhami3310.Impression   (USB image writer)
#   page.tesk.Refine                  (GNOME internals tweaker)
#   com.ranfdev.DistroShelf           (distrobox GUI)
# These are the Bluefin-list entries svk drops on purpose: each one hands a student
# (or a teacher-installed-for-a-student) a way around the lockdown or the disk.
#
# One app id per line. Fleet-wide additions belong here + a rebuild; a teacher's
# per-machine install goes through gnome-software and stays on that machine.
org.mozilla.firefox
org.gnome.TextEditor
org.gnome.Calculator
org.gnome.Papers
org.gnome.Loupe
org.gnome.FileRoller
org.libreoffice.LibreOffice
org.gimp.GIMP
org.inkscape.Inkscape
org.audacityteam.Audacity
org.videolan.VLC
org.gnome.gitlab.YaLTeR.VideoTrimmer
org.openshot.OpenShot
no.mifi.losslesscut
org.gtk.Gtk3theme.adw-gtk3
org.gtk.Gtk3theme.adw-gtk3-dark
